WEBVTT

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:11.990
A class reunion sounds nice.

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:15.170
It's even in the gymnasium 
of your old school.

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:16.990
There's something authentic about that.

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:21.750
Fool. I fail to see how there's 
anything good about this nonsense.

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:26.250
Listen up. A class reunion is, 
when you get down to it,

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:30.800
nothing but a chance for people who are 
trapped in the past to escape reality.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:32.620
O-Okay.

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:35.800
Then why are you going, Tonegawa-sensei?

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:39.470
To confirm a few things.

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:40.560
Confirm what?

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:44.790
When they were young, 
these people had the nerve to talk big,

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:47.560
despite being nothing more than 
self-indulgent, unproductive scum...

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:51.140
So what exactly has become of them?

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:55.940
We're here, eh?

00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:57.320
Yes, sir.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:17.010
<b>Middle Management Blues</b>

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:17.010
<b><i>Mr. Tonegawa</i></b>

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:42.800
<i>Agenda 23
<b></b></i>\h\h\h\h\h\h\hPremonition

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:41.340
<b>15th Graduating Class Reunion</b>

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:45.600
<b>Donation - Tonegawa Yukio</b>

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:48.850
<b>Reception</b>

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:48.850
<b>Class 3</b>

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:48.850
<b>Class 3</b>

00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:48.850
<i>Shortly after arriving at the venue...</i>

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:51.320
Huh? Yukki?

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:53.670
Hey, it <i>is</i> you, Yukki!

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:57.000
It's me, remember? Ueno!

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.320
Man, it's been a long time!

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:01.860
<b>Caught!</b>

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:01.860
<i>He's caught by a friend 
who's obnoxiously loud!</i>

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:05.660
Damn it, of all the people to find me...

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:09.090
Yes! That venom! I knew it was you, Yukki!

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:11.870
I read your column in that financial paper!

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.630
"Money is worth more than life."

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:22.150
"People don't live provisional lives." 
"If you don't win, you're trash!"

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:26.640
And the best one was, "No more—"

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:27.140
Stop that! Drop it already!

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:29.980
Pretty impressive!

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:32.050
I told you to drop it...

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:40.900
<b>An overwhelming assumption of intimacy!!</b>

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.810
<i>An overwhelming assumption of intimacy!</i>

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:38.970
<i>Even the maxims of Teiai's number-two 
man are fodder for mockery,</i>

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:40.900
<i>when confronted with his classmates!</i>

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:43.160
Yahoo!

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:45.660
Hey, Shinanogawa!

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:52.330
Here we go! It's the raging rivers duo!

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:52.920
<b>Raging Rivers Duo</b>

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:56.520
<i>The longest river in Japan, Shinanogawa!</i>

00:03:54.770 --> 00:04:01.670
Shinanogawa

00:03:57.460 --> 00:04:00.610
<i>And the river with the greatest 
surface area in Japan, Tonegawa!</i>

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:01.670
Tonegawa

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:03.430
Okay, smile now!

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:06.690
Stop it! Don't assume I'm part 
of some unit with this ass!

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:08.180
That venom!

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:11.430
Hey, it's the raging rivers duo.

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:13.310
Nakabeppu!

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:16.470
And you're as loud as ever, huh, Ueno?

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:19.940
<i>The old friends gather, one after another!</i>

00:04:20.390 --> 00:04:21.940
<i>Good grief...</i>

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:25.950
<i>Acting like high school kids at their age?</i>

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:29.790
<i>The worse someone's actual life is going,</i>

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:32.340
<i>the more they tend to act 
out at these things.</i>

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:36.740
<i>Nakabeppu, who said he was 
going to become a model,</i>

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:39.670
<i>is wearing a ragged suit now.</i>

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:43.330
<i>Then there's Shinanogawa, 
who wanted to become a singer.</i>

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:46.490
<i>Who knows what he's doing now?</i>

00:04:46.490 --> 00:04:48.470
<i>It's as Tonegawa said...</i>

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:51.480
<i>In contrast to those 
who are making a big fuss,</i>

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:56.920
<i>those who have had successful lives 
are calmly having a friendly chat.</i>

00:04:58.340 --> 00:04:59.690
<i>Not only that,</i>

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:02.010
<i>but some of them are 
even trying to network.</i>

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:10.070
<i>It seems that not a single 
one of them has changed.</i>

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:14.760
<i>The people who've worked hard have 
had their measures of success,</i>

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:16.810
<i>and the idiots remain idiots.</i>

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:22.500
<i>The only thing that seems to have changed 
is that everyone has aged appropriately.</i>

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:27.930
<i>The baby-faced Yamamoto, who had older 
girls telling him how cute he was,</i>

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:30.510
<b>Yamamoto</b>

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:30.510
<i>has hair growing out of his ears.</i>

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:34.730
<i>Yabe from the soccer club, who was 
handsome and popular with the girls,</i>

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:39.020
<b>Yabe</b>

00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:39.020
<i>is going bald. Even if his 
face has held together.</i>

00:05:39.490 --> 00:05:42.820
<i>Okamura, who was dating Yabe back then,</i>

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:48.030
<b>Okamura</b>

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:48.030
<i>has changed a lot, but still has 
the same Matsuda Seiko haircut.</i>

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:52.290
<i>How cruel the passage of time is...</i>

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:54.970
Oh! Yukio-kun?

00:05:56.760 --> 00:05:59.320
That is you, isn't it?

00:06:02.180 --> 00:06:05.670
K-Kagawa Maho!

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:08.610
Kagawa Maho

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:08.610
<b>Maho... Maho... Maho...</b>

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:12.520
Come on, why the full name, Yukio-kun?

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:13.810
Uh, I just...

00:06:14.230 --> 00:06:17.140
No need to be so formal. 
Treat me like in the old days.

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:19.060
Or you could call me Maho-Maho!

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:23.590
<b>Maho-Maho... Maho-Maho...</b>

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:27.410
Fool. Neither of us is young enough 
for that kind of thing anymore.

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:31.570
So harsh! I see you still 
have that same old venom!

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:32.570
Shut it!

00:06:33.510 --> 00:06:34.330
<i>Glance...</i>

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:39.080
Still, the both of us sure have
grown old, haven't we?

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:42.630
Yes, I suppose so.

00:06:43.010 --> 00:06:44.130
Maho!

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:46.040
Oh, coming!

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:48.720
Well, I'll talk to you later, Yukio-kun.

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:49.730
Right.

00:06:50.290 --> 00:06:51.800
Sorry for the wait.

00:07:05.430 --> 00:07:07.530
<i>In the summer of their 
second year of high school...</i>

00:07:07.910 --> 00:07:09.140
Yukio-kun!

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:18.150
Um... well... I... I've always...

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:22.810
<i>Kagawa Maho confesses her 
feelings to Tonegawa,</i>

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:26.530
<i>and is rejected.</i>

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:30.070
<i>That being the case,</i>

00:07:30.070 --> 00:07:34.300
<i>you would assume that Tonegawa 
didn't have much affection for her.</i>

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:39.000
<i>And he didn't, but in spite of that, 
when he saw her wedding ring...</i>

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:42.840
<i>Tonegawa was mildly shocked.</i>

00:07:50.930 --> 00:07:51.930
A ball?

00:07:53.850 --> 00:07:55.570
Why's there a ball?

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:00.080
Okay, here's my chance! Take this!

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:00.790
Ow!

00:08:03.320 --> 00:08:04.370
What the?

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:07.120
Ooh! Yabe-kun!

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:08.670
Looking good, Shinacchi!

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:11.840
Wait, hold it, time out! 
I'm sorry, I'm sorry!

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:13.680
Blammo!

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:15.930
Cowabunga!

00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:21.920
<i>These imbeciles... Now they're 
acting more like grade schoolers!</i>

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:24.440
<i>Anyone can see they're 
getting too out of hand!</i>

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:26.740
Goodness...

00:08:27.160 --> 00:08:32.250
They're a helpless bunch, aren't they? 
They're acting like kids.

00:08:32.250 --> 00:08:33.320
Kagawa...

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:36.920
Ueno-kun brought up the idea,

00:08:36.920 --> 00:08:38.960
and everyone went along with it.

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:42.750
Oh, you have a ball. Did you want to play, too?

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:44.330
No! This is just...

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:47.960
Kagawa-san!

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:49.210
Look out!

00:08:56.070 --> 00:08:57.970
Yukio-kun!

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:12.730
You can enjoy yourselves, 
but don't go overboard.

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:24.150
Oh, Yamazaki?

00:09:24.150 --> 00:09:26.750
Yeah. I'm ready to be picked up.

00:09:34.660 --> 00:09:36.260
Yukio-kun!

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:44.980
Um... Our teachers are going 
to be showing up soon.

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:49.400
We're all going to sing the school song, 
apparently. Why don't you join us?

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:53.400
This is asinine. I'm leaving.

00:09:55.370 --> 00:09:59.190
Playing dodgeball... 
Singing the school song...

00:09:59.190 --> 00:10:01.170
It's embarrassing to see 
adults acting like this.

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:05.160
We're not high school students anymore.

00:10:07.030 --> 00:10:07.790
Yes...

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:12.290
You have a point, Yukio-kun. 
It is a bit embarrassing.

00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:13.670
But...

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:16.420
Isn't it also fun?

00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:21.510
To take just one day to...

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:23.180
That venom!

00:10:26.610 --> 00:10:28.660
...act the way we used to?

00:10:33.030 --> 00:10:35.190
You can keep asking me, 
but my answer won't change.

00:10:35.670 --> 00:10:38.370
I am not singing!

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:48.460
We now take wing, our youthful hearts abeat

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:57.060
Dedicated in pursuit of knowledge, 
for we are students

00:10:57.060 --> 00:11:05.390
The infinite clouds float in the sky above

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:13.700
Painting visions of who we will be someday

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:17.830
When we take flight, where will we go?

00:11:17.830 --> 00:11:21.410
With the wind at our backs, pushing us along

00:11:19.380 --> 00:11:21.410
<i>Despite his protests,</i>

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:26.240
<i>Tonegawa ends up enjoying his class reunion!</i>

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:29.780
Our hearts continue to shine

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:34.050
Now, take flight, take flight!

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:39.010
<b>15th Graduating Class Reunion</b>

00:11:34.050 --> 00:11:36.530
<i>See you in ten years!</i>

00:11:34.050 --> 00:11:38.260
In the name of our school!

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:43.840
Money is worth more than life!

00:11:46.490 --> 00:11:50.020
<i>Ootsuki and Numakawa are released!</i>

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:54.270
Man, I'm really looking forward to this!

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:56.550
I'm gonna eat all kinds of tasty food,

00:11:56.550 --> 00:11:59.030
and tomorrow, we'll go to the 
place I've been wanting to visit...

00:11:59.380 --> 00:12:03.280
The board game café! 
Or, board gafé for short!

00:12:03.280 --> 00:12:06.930
We're gonna have so much fun! I can't wait!

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:09.790
Huh? Foreman, what's wrong?

00:12:10.130 --> 00:12:12.770
I'm sorry, Numakawa, but I think...

00:12:13.190 --> 00:12:17.290
I'm coming down with something!

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:20.320
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:12:20.530 --> 00:12:25.010
No fever yet, and I'm not feeling 
particularly bad, but...

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:30.020
I've got this faint feeling of twitchiness 
going on between my nose and throat.

00:12:27.240 --> 00:12:30.290
<b>Twitch...</b>

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:34.080
C-Come on, that's no 
guarantee you'll get sick!

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:35.940
I can tell!

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:41.030
If there's a button that gives 
me a cold when pressed,

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:45.450
then right now, someone is tracing 
the edge of it as we speak.

00:12:45.900 --> 00:12:48.550
There's no telling when it might be pressed.

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:53.080
Uh, I don't really follow, but...

00:12:53.390 --> 00:12:55.940
Why did it have to be today?!

00:12:55.940 --> 00:12:59.260
If there's one day when an underground 
laborer shouldn't get sick,

00:12:59.260 --> 00:13:00.630
it's during an excursion!

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:02.680
It's not like you to let this happen!

00:13:02.680 --> 00:13:03.720
If I had to guess...

00:13:05.460 --> 00:13:07.100
I must've caught a chill

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:10.630
when I was left out on the bench!

00:13:11.050 --> 00:13:14.230
An unexpected pitfall in the 
one-day excursion setup!

00:13:16.250 --> 00:13:18.440
For now, let's split up.

00:13:19.830 --> 00:13:22.240
You don't want to catch 
whatever this is, do you?

00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:24.650
W-Well, I don't, but...

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:25.860
Don't worry.

00:13:26.520 --> 00:13:30.370
I'll fix this! And I'll do it in time 
for the board games tomorrow!

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:38.880
<i>He will? How's he going to do that?</i>

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:42.380
<i>After that, Ootsuki...</i>

00:13:43.010 --> 00:13:46.060
<i>cancels his reservation at a cheap hotel</i>

00:13:46.060 --> 00:13:47.880
<i>and arranges different lodging.</i>

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:50.890
<b>Super Matsuno</b>

00:13:48.950 --> 00:13:50.890
<i>He heads to a nearby supermarket,</i>

00:13:51.330 --> 00:13:53.640
<i>where he buys onions, ginger, and eggs,</i>

00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:57.130
<i>along with pork and other groceries.</i>

00:13:57.640 --> 00:14:01.400
<i>He also picks up a change of clothes 
and some lozenges at DanQui.</i>

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:07.650
<i>Here we are! This is the place.</i>

00:14:08.120 --> 00:14:11.320
<i>Rental apartments where you 
can stay for just one night.</i>

00:14:16.600 --> 00:14:20.670
<i>And the difference between 
this place and a hotel is...</i>

00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:24.170
<i>This place has a kitchen with a sink!</i>

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:27.340
<i>Not only that, but it's 
got the utensils, as well.</i>

00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:29.180
<i>All the essentials are here.</i>

00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:32.180
<i>And...</i>

00:14:32.620 --> 00:14:36.770
Looks like I wasn't wrong after all!

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:41.960
<i>Now then, before the fever 
starts to get serious...</i>

00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:44.070
<i>I should get down to business.</i>

00:14:45.010 --> 00:14:48.990
<i>Cut the onions and ginger 
to prepare the base!</i>

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:52.720
<i>Minced pork with plenty of ginger</i>

00:14:52.720 --> 00:14:57.000
<i>and a dash of yuzu peel, which actually 
contains more vitamins than the fruit itself.</i>

00:14:57.380 --> 00:15:00.320
<i>Then add salt and pepper to taste!</i>

00:15:00.320 --> 00:15:01.250
<i>And now...</i>

00:15:03.860 --> 00:15:07.220
<i>You knead it, knowing that the 
more you do, the tastier it'll be!</i>

00:15:07.890 --> 00:15:10.860
<i>The need to knead!</i>

00:15:10.860 --> 00:15:13.760
<i>And then, just as it's coming to a boil...</i>

00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:16.390
<i>Make it rain meatballs!</i>

00:15:16.390 --> 00:15:19.390
Once everything is heated up, 
we add the veggies!

00:15:19.390 --> 00:15:21.650
<b>1 Hour Later</b>

00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:24.710
And it's done...

00:15:24.710 --> 00:15:29.300
My special meatball hotpot loaded 
with green onions and ginger!

00:15:30.550 --> 00:15:32.450
<i>Now, then...</i>

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:36.580
<i>Grab a well-soaked onion and
a meatball full of ginger,</i>

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:39.200
<i>dip it into some ponzu 
with grated daikon, and...</i>

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:46.460
So good!

00:15:46.950 --> 00:15:51.720
<i>I wasn't sure this would work since 
I don't have much of an appetite,</i>

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:54.720
<i>but a single bite was enough 
to wash those worries away!</i>

00:15:55.410 --> 00:15:57.720
<i>And now I can't control my appetite!</i>

00:16:01.690 --> 00:16:03.020
<i>Thanks to this hotpot,</i>

00:16:03.910 --> 00:16:06.480
<i>Ootsuki's body temperature rises,</i>

00:16:06.970 --> 00:16:10.490
<i>leading to intense perspiration! 
Not only that, but...</i>

00:16:06.970 --> 00:16:10.490
<b>Heat...</b>

00:16:11.330 --> 00:16:15.450
<i>The efficiently digested nutrients, 
such as vitamins and proteins,</i>

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:20.120
<i>circulate through Ootsuki's 
body on a casual trip,</i>

00:16:20.840 --> 00:16:24.370
<i>disembarking at all the 
cells throughout his body.</i>

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:31.540
Who could that be?

00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:34.260
Numakawa shouldn't know where I am...

00:16:36.170 --> 00:16:37.250
Yes?

00:16:39.170 --> 00:16:41.140
Miyamoto-san?

00:16:41.140 --> 00:16:41.850
Hey.

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:44.070
Huh? The way you're dressed...

00:16:44.820 --> 00:16:46.350
I'm actually off today.

00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:51.610
I was walking around and saw one of the other 
men in black, and when I talked to him,

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:53.990
he told me it looked like you were sick.

00:16:54.580 --> 00:16:57.240
So I rushed over to bring you some umeboshi.

00:16:58.500 --> 00:17:00.740
Oh, I can't possibly accept these...

00:17:00.740 --> 00:17:03.750
It's fine. My family sent them to me.

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:05.750
<b>Later...</b>

00:17:04.130 --> 00:17:05.750
<i>Later...</i>

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:07.250
Cheers!

00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:13.010
<i>They knock back a bit of eggnog with sake
while snacking on umeboshi.</i>

00:17:14.100 --> 00:17:18.440
I'm relieved, though. 
Seems like you're not doing too bad.

00:17:19.110 --> 00:17:21.940
You don't get it at all, Miyamoto-san.

00:17:21.510 --> 00:17:23.430
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:17:23.430 --> 00:17:26.720
If I relaxed now, I'd be a failure.

00:17:26.720 --> 00:17:31.550
A failure at getting better. 
When convalescing, you have to go all-in!

00:17:31.550 --> 00:17:35.610
Tomorrow only comes for those 
who put in the effort today!

00:17:36.050 --> 00:17:37.200
<b>Psst... Psst.. Psst...</b>

00:17:40.570 --> 00:17:43.490
Hey, Ootsuki, is this what you meant?

00:17:43.490 --> 00:17:45.120
Yeah, that's perfect.

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:49.720
You stick rolled up newspapers 
into a bucket filled with water.

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:54.710
Doing this creates an improvised humidifier!

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:54.710
<b>Improvised humidifier!!</b>

00:17:54.710 --> 00:17:56.820
How many more do you need?

00:17:56.820 --> 00:17:58.470
Four more should do.

00:18:01.850 --> 00:18:05.980
<i>After assisting in Ootsuki's convalescence 
for a while, Miyamoto heads home.</i>

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:13.360
<i>Now, it's about time to sleep 
using the special method.</i>

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:18.990
<i>Ootsuki wraps his blanket 
around both sides of his body,</i>

00:18:19.810 --> 00:18:22.740
<i>folding the portion at 
his feet to seal him in!</i>

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:27.750
<i>It is now complete! 
The 100% secure Ootsuki Roll!</i>

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:28.250
<b>Completed!</b>

00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:28.250
<b>Ootsuki Roll!!</b>

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:30.650
<i>Goodnight.</i>

00:18:36.210 --> 00:18:37.480
Morning!

00:18:37.480 --> 00:18:38.200
Good morning!

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:39.720
Good morning!

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:40.200
Did you do your homework?

00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:41.300
Yep, I did.

00:18:44.120 --> 00:18:48.480
<i>The innocent voices of children on their 
way to school make for a quiet awakening.</i>

00:18:48.840 --> 00:18:52.860
<i>I'm soaked through with sweat, 
and my vision is sharp!</i>

00:18:54.680 --> 00:18:57.290
<i>I don't even need a thermometer to tell...</i>

00:18:57.290 --> 00:19:00.610
<i>Right now my temperature is 36.4°!</i>

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:02.370
<i>Afterward...</i>

00:19:02.710 --> 00:19:05.120
<i>He takes a leisurely bath with some yuzu,</i>

00:19:05.510 --> 00:19:07.620
<i>and after changing into 
a fresh set of clothes,</i>

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:13.130
<i>he heats up last night's hotpot leftovers, 
then adds some washed rice to it.</i>

00:19:13.700 --> 00:19:16.880
<i>Then he adds some scrambled egg...</i>

00:19:17.370 --> 00:19:21.380
<i>And it's done: rice gruel with egg!</i>

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:25.240
So good!

00:19:26.530 --> 00:19:30.970
<i>With his appetite fully restored, 
Ootsuki eats like a champ!</i>

00:19:32.530 --> 00:19:35.150
<i>In no time, he finishes the whole bowl!</i>

00:19:36.600 --> 00:19:38.280
My body feels light!

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:41.280
I'm fully recovered!

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:44.280
<i>I've still got time before I need to leave,</i>

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:47.110
<i>so maybe I'll take a walk 
around the neighborhood...</i>

00:19:48.660 --> 00:19:50.850
<i>...is what I pretend to do, but then...</i>

00:19:50.850 --> 00:19:53.640
<i>Bed! In!</i>

00:19:56.760 --> 00:20:01.930
I bet the last bits of virus in 
my body just got their hopes up!

00:20:02.370 --> 00:20:05.180
Sorry, but I'm not showing any mercy!

00:20:05.180 --> 00:20:07.810
<i>I'll use a three-hour roll 
to finish things up...</i>

00:20:07.810 --> 00:20:10.630
<i>To take care of every last one of them!</i>

00:20:09.890 --> 00:20:12.060
<b>3 Hour</b>

00:20:10.390 --> 00:20:12.060
<b>Ootsuki Roll!!</b>

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:23.010
<i>It's almost time to start 
playing board games...</i>

00:20:23.010 --> 00:20:25.400
<i>Is the foreman gonna make it?</i>

00:20:25.400 --> 00:20:27.580
Numakawa!

00:20:31.780 --> 00:20:33.330
Yoohoo!

00:20:33.780 --> 00:20:35.370
Foreman!

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:38.090
<b>Ultimately...</b>

00:20:36.600 --> 00:20:38.090
<i>Ultimately...</i>

00:20:38.440 --> 00:20:40.340
<i>On this day, Ootsuki...</i>

00:20:40.740 --> 00:20:43.640
That card doesn't count!

00:20:44.230 --> 00:20:46.340
The foreman wins again?!

00:20:46.680 --> 00:20:50.850
<i>He's even more energetic than usual
as he enjoys the board games!</i>

00:20:51.620 --> 00:20:54.230
<i>Skip one turn, but then jump six spaces.</i>

00:20:58.260 --> 00:21:00.460
<i>Miyamoto ends up catching the crud</i>

00:21:00.460 --> 00:21:02.590
<i>and is forced to take a 
shocking amount of time off.</i>

00:21:02.590 --> 00:21:05.740
<i>Six days... using his vacation time!</i>

00:21:06.420 --> 00:21:08.460
I gotta get better soon,

00:21:08.460 --> 00:21:13.000
or I won't be able to join 
Ootsuki on his next excursion—

00:21:13.410 --> 00:21:19.220
<i>Foreman Ootsuki! Where will his 
next one-day excursion take him?</i>

00:22:55.160 --> 00:22:57.780
Next time, "Obsession."

00:22:56.470 --> 00:23:00.250
<b>Obsession</b>
